<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle up $1-$3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle up $1-$3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers sold $1.00-$3.00 per cwt higher, compared to last Thursday, USDA said. Demand very good. Offerings attractive consisting of native and western orgin backgrounded steers and heifers with many fleshy offerings included.</p>
<p>Many cattleman electing to take advantage of the premium on fleshy two-way steers and heifers over the fed cattle market. 94 percent over 600 lbs</p>
<p>Steers - Medium and Large 1 - Small consignment 468 lbs 103.00; 500-600 lbs 90.25-96.00; 600-700 lbs 82.00-88.25; 700-750 lbs 82.60-83.25; 800-900 lbs 73.75-78.90; 900-1000 lbs 72.60-75.50; 1000-1100 lbs 67.80-73.50; 1100- 1175 lbs many fleshy 66.40-68.50.</p>
<p>Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - Few 400-450 lbs 83.50-88.00; 500-600 lbs 79.50-80.25; 650-700 lbs 77.25-78.10; 700-800 lbs 73.50-76.75; 800-900 lbs 69.25-72.70; 900-1000 lbs some fleshy 66.60-69.50; 1000-1100 lbs fleshy 63.70-67.75. Receipts - This Week 3,100 Last Week 2,125 Last Year 1,875</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
